**CSS + minimal HTML to create a rotating “card” on hover**

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* Container – keeps the card centered */
.card-wrapper {
  perspective: 1000px;          /* gives depth for 3D effect */
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  margin: 50px auto;
}

/* The card itself */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  background: #fff;
  border-radius: 12px;
  box-shadow: 0 10px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
  transition: transform .6s ease;   /* smooth rotation */
  transform-style: preserve-3d;     /* allow children to be 3D */
  position: relative;
}

/* Hover effect – rotate around Y‑axis */
.card:hover {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);       /* change to rotateX or rotateZ if you prefer */
}

/* Front & back faces */
.card::before,
.card::after {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  backface-visibility: hidden;     /* hide backside when rotated */
  border-radius: 12px;
}

.card::before {                     /* front face */
  background: linear-gradient(135deg,#ff9a9e 0%,#fad0c4 100%);
  display:flex;
  align-items:center;
  justify-content:center;
  font-size:1.5rem;
  color:#fff;
}

.card::after {                      /* back face */
  background: linear-gradient(135deg,#a18cd1 0%,#fbc2eb 100%);
  transform: rotateY(180deg);      /* flip it so it shows on reverse side */
  display:flex;
  align-items:center;
  justify-content:center;
  font-size:1.5rem;
  color:#fff;
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card"></div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Element | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `.card-wrapper` | Sets `perspective` to give a 3D feel. |
| `.card` | Holds the card content, has a transition for smooth animation. |
| `transform-style: preserve-3d` | Allows child elements (`::before`, `::after`) to maintain 3D positioning. |
| `backface-visibility: hidden` | Hides the backside of each face during rotation. |
| `::before` / `::after` | Represent the front and back faces of the card. The back face is rotated 180° so it appears when the card flips. |

Feel free to replace the gradient backgrounds with images or text. Adjust the `rotateY(180deg)` to `rotateX(180deg)` or `rotateZ(180deg)` if you want a different axis of rotation. Enjoy your rotating card!
